@startuml elo_dockerised_mvp
title elo — CV, Career, Assessment and Roadmap adviser
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #285F91
skinparam nodeBackgroundColor #F4F8FC
skinparam nodeBorderColor #8DA6BC
skinparam componentBackgroundColor white
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #EFF6FA

actor "User browser" as Browser
component "Existing Profile / account APIs\nAuthentication, onboarding, planning inputs\nAccount-owned manual capability declarations" as Profile
cloud "Configured CV model API\nOpenAI-compatible extraction, routing and interpretation" as CVLLM
cloud "Career model router\nGemini 3.5 Flash Lite: extraction / reasoning / edits\nSame Gemini client: chat + research coordination" as LLM
cloud "Brave LLM Context API\nConfigured API access required" as Sources

node "Docker Compose — focused design" {
  node "Next.js / React / TypeScript" as Web <<Docker container>>
  node "NGINX API gateway" as Gateway <<Docker container>>

  package "Private backend network" {
    node "CV analyser\nservices/cv-service" as CV <<Docker container>> {
      artifact "Saved upload/review and resumable text chat\nSource-linked clarification, correction and selection\n/api/v1/cv" as CVAPI
    }
    node "Career goal and public research\nservices/career-service" as Career <<Docker container>> {
      artifact "Specific JD or conversational discovery\nOne canonical CareerGoal + explicit CV confirmation\nStructured skills and five-category Opportunity Intelligence\nScoped Q&A with projected MongoDB retrieval\n/api/v1/career" as CareerAPI
    }
    node "Private capability assessment\nservices/assessment-service" as Assessment <<Docker container>> {
      artifact "Version-pinned comparison and source evidence\nSeparate role, interview and constraint outcomes\n/api/v1/assessments" as AssessmentAPI
    }
    node "Roadmap and task service\nservices/roadmap-service" as Roadmap <<Docker container>> {
      artifact "Saved adviser chat beside proposed/active plan\nChosen days, daily workload and task history\n/api/v1/roadmaps" as RoadmapAPI
    }
  }

  node "MongoDB — local development" as Mongo <<Docker container>> {
    database "CV-owned database\ncvs\ncv_selections + cv_conversations (operational)\ncv_upload_capacity + cv_model_usage (operational)" as CVDB
    database "Career-owned database\ncareer_goals + career_state (operational)\ninterview_research" as CareerDB
    database "Assessment-owned database\nskill_gap_analyses\nworkspaces with batch checkpoints" as AssessmentDB
    database "Roadmap-owned database\nroadmaps immutable revisions\nworkspaces with chat and active/draft" as RoadmapDB
  }
  artifact "Service-private temporary CV storage\nQuota admission, shared POSIX locks and recoverable cleanup" as Uploads <<Private storage>>
}

Browser --> Web : Use application
Web --> Gateway : /api/v1 requests
Gateway --> Profile : Existing account / profile routes
Gateway --> CV : Saved CV and conversation routes
Gateway --> Career : Career routes
Gateway --> Assessment : Assessment owner routes
Gateway --> Roadmap : Adviser and tasks

' API dependencies point from caller to the service it calls.
CV --> Profile : Validate session / read declarations / confirmed additions
Profile --> CV : Validate explicit source attachment
CV --> Career : Current confirmed goal/version/selection projection
Career --> Profile : Validate session / read selected context
Career --> CV : Read effective CV skills and extraction version
Roadmap --> Profile : Read deadline and availability
Assessment --> CV : Selected effective evidence and versions
Assessment --> Career : Full goal and linked research snapshot
Assessment --> Profile : Verify session and current background
Roadmap --> Assessment : Current comparison and freshness

CV --> CVDB : Own records only
Career --> CareerDB : Own records only
Assessment --> AssessmentDB : Own records only
Roadmap --> RoadmapDB : Own records only
CV --> Uploads : Temporary original access
CV --> CVLLM : Bounded extraction, routing and interpretation
Career --> LLM : Goal interpretation / scoped chat / cited research synthesis
Career --> Sources : LangGraph parallel LLM Context research branches
Assessment --> LLM : Service-scoped evidence interpretation
Roadmap --> LLM : Service-scoped adviser recommendations

note bottom of Career
  One career_goals model: specific_job or career_exploration.
  CV acknowledgement binds the exact current goal/version/selection.
  Automatic goal saves do not silently confirm CV context.
  company may be null. Interview research is reusable public context;
  private CV/chat data must not enter that shared research.
  Validate job identity; overlap full JD extraction with public-only retrieval.
  Matching early evidence seeds the existing research job after goal saving.
  Cards update on extraction; chat retains observed activity until both results succeed.
  Gemini writes one cited overview from JD details and completed research.
  Temporary observed activity disappears on completion; scoped follow-up chat can search Brave.
  Persist structured output and bounded evidence, not full raw JD text.
  JD originals/previews use service-private temporary parsing storage.
end note

note bottom of Mongo
  Separate service-owned databases and credentials.
  No cross-service collection queries; use authenticated APIs.
  Production may replace local MongoDB with MongoDB Atlas.
  The users collection in the UML maps to the existing
  Profile/account authority outside this diagram's three-service scope.
end note

legend bottom
  Focused design direction, not a deployment or implementation claim.
  Core scope: CV, Career, separate Assessment and Roadmap adviser.
  Existing Profile/auth is shown only as an external dependency.
  Dashboard, review/scheduling and future services are intentionally omitted;
  extend this diagram when their scope is agreed.
  Current implementation: Profile/auth, temporary Career JD previews,
  optional-CV exploration, one autosaved current goal/chat, LangGraph research, saved CV upload/review/chat and data contracts.
  Importance review, advisory skills and versioned research orchestration/review are implemented.
  Brave retrieval exclusively uses LLM Context; historical AI answer attribution remains readable.
  Source-linked CV interpretation is implemented; Assessment comparison and Roadmap adviser are implemented with synthetic verification; live quality remains unverified.
  Synthetic tests do not establish live-provider quality or deployed readiness.
  career_state (including version-bound CV acknowledgement) and research_contexts are operational metadata.
  career_checkpoints / career_checkpoint_writes retain safe graph state for 24h.
  Gemini/Brave provider quotas and task context/output/time limits remain enforced.
  Opportunity Intelligence embeds typed categories/findings/summary in interview_research.
  Durable category jobs/receipts reuse research_contexts; no duplicate domain collections.
  Gemini plans, evaluates cited evidence and selects validated summaries using unchanged JSON models.
  Collection and embedded-object schemas: sibling mongodb_*.mmd files.
endlegend
@enduml
